1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,362
Two instruction manuals.

2
00:00:02,362 --> 00:00:06,589
One thousand six hundred and twenty-three scanned pages.

3
00:00:06,589 --> 00:00:09,458
And not a single searchable character.

4
00:00:09,458 --> 00:00:12,931
Finding one safety rule could take an evening.

5
00:00:12,931 --> 00:00:15,271
This is the problem PDF Q and A

6
00:00:15,271 --> 00:00:16,630
was built to kill.

7
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:19,623
This is PDF Q and A.

8
00:00:19,623 --> 00:00:23,162
Drop in any PDF, even a thousand-page scanned

9
00:00:23,162 --> 00:00:27,016
manual, and it reads every page, saves everything

10
00:00:27,016 --> 00:00:30,791
into a database, and answers your questions with

11
00:00:30,791 --> 00:00:32,522
the exact page number.

12
00:00:32,522 --> 00:00:33,229
No cloud.

13
00:00:33,229 --> 00:00:34,488
No subscription.

14
00:00:34,488 --> 00:00:36,690
It runs on your own machine.

15
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:41,536
Uploading is drag and drop, up to twenty

16
00:00:41,536 --> 00:00:42,581
files at once.

17
00:00:42,581 --> 00:00:45,866
Scanned pages are read locally by Rapid OCR,

18
00:00:45,866 --> 00:00:48,554
and you watch every page land in the

19
00:00:48,554 --> 00:00:49,599
database live:

20
00:00:49,599 --> 00:00:52,585
page number, percentage, time remaining.

21
00:00:52,585 --> 00:00:54,750
Nothing leaves your computer.

22
00:00:56,550 --> 00:00:57,133
Now ask.

23
00:00:57,133 --> 00:00:59,900
The answer comes back with its source:

24
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:02,594
the file name, the page number, and a

25
00:01:02,594 --> 00:01:03,467
match score.

26
00:01:03,467 --> 00:01:06,307
Open the sources and you are looking at

27
00:01:06,307 --> 00:01:09,001
the exact passage the database found.

28
00:01:09,001 --> 00:01:11,550
You can verify everything yourself.

29
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:14,719
Here is the pipeline.

30
00:01:14,719 --> 00:01:17,817
The browser talks to an Express server.

31
00:01:17,817 --> 00:01:21,234
A Python worker extracts text with PyMuPDF;

32
00:01:21,234 --> 00:01:24,015
scanned pages go through Rapid OCR.

33
00:01:24,015 --> 00:01:27,750
Prisma writes every page and chunk into SQLite,

34
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:30,054
with an FTS5 full-text index.

35
00:01:30,054 --> 00:01:33,312
A question runs a BM25 search first, then

36
00:01:33,312 --> 00:01:36,490
builds the answer from the top passages.

37
00:01:38,050 --> 00:01:39,514
Then the AI chain.

38
00:01:39,514 --> 00:01:43,418
Ollama runs first, entirely on your own machine.

39
00:01:43,418 --> 00:01:47,078
Then GLM, NVIDIA NIM, OpenRouter, and Gemini.

40
00:01:47,078 --> 00:01:50,657
If one provider fails, the next one answers.

41
00:01:50,657 --> 00:01:54,073
And if every provider fails, you still get

42
00:01:54,073 --> 00:01:55,699
the database answer.

43
00:01:55,699 --> 00:01:57,570
The system never stops.

44
00:01:59,050 --> 00:02:02,348
Libraries and models, exactly as shipped.

45
00:02:02,348 --> 00:02:04,278
Node twenty and Express.

46
00:02:04,278 --> 00:02:07,174
Prisma seven with the libSQL driver.

47
00:02:07,174 --> 00:02:10,632
SQLite with an FTS5 index and BM25 ranking.

48
00:02:10,632 --> 00:02:12,884
PyMuPDF for text and layout.

49
00:02:12,884 --> 00:02:14,975
Rapid OCR on ONNX Runtime.

50
00:02:14,975 --> 00:02:18,997
Ollama runs Qwen two point five, seven B, locally.

51
00:02:18,997 --> 00:02:22,134
The cloud chain is GLM four point seven

52
00:02:22,134 --> 00:02:27,121
Flash, NVIDIA Nemotron three point five Lightning, OpenRouter,

53
00:02:27,121 --> 00:02:28,890
and Gemini Flash Lite.

54
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:32,305
Your data stays yours.

55
00:02:32,305 --> 00:02:35,258
View any page, export to text, CSV or

56
00:02:35,258 --> 00:02:37,891
JSON, delete with a confirmation.

57
00:02:37,891 --> 00:02:40,365
The whole app works on a phone.

58
00:02:40,365 --> 00:02:44,115
And a complete Docker plus EC2 deployment guide

59
00:02:44,115 --> 00:02:46,030
ships in the repository.

60
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:49,320
Setup is one command.

61
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,668
Run one command.

62
00:02:50,668 --> 00:02:52,690
Then drop a PDF and ask.

63
00:02:52,690 --> 00:02:56,229
The full guide, the Word documents and the

64
00:02:56,229 --> 00:02:58,505
code are in the repository.

65
00:02:58,505 --> 00:03:00,190
Thanks for watching.

